+  `r_LensChromaticAberration` exactly like `r_LensDistortion` (new `m_savedLensChromatic`
+  member, captured under the same `m_bLensCharSaved` latch). Editor-live like the other lens
+  character cvars. Push `Dof_User_FieldCurvature` / `Dof_User_EdgeSoftness` in `ApplyDOF`
+  with save / restore like `Dof_User_CatEye`.
+
+## 4. Acceptance
+
+1. All three at 0: pixel-identical to today (`ComputeCircleOfConfusion` reduces to the old
+   formula, `ca = 0` skips the two samples).
+2. Field Curvature +1, f/1.4, camera square to a textured wall focused at the centre: the
+   wall's edges blur (far layer), the centre stays sharp; f/8 brings them back. -1 inverts the
+   direction of the focus error (the edges go sharp when the centre is focused slightly behind
+   the wall).
+3. Edge Softness 1 wide open: the corners are unmistakably soft with the whole frame in focus;
+   f/5.6 (p ≈ 0.25 → p² ≈ 0.06) makes it nearly vanish.
+4. Chromatic Aberration 1: bright/dark edges near the frame border show red on the outer side,
+   cyan on the inner; the centre is clean. With squeeze 2× and distortion 0.5 the fringes follow
+   the remapped picture (no ghost, no double image). SMAA 2TX / TSAA sharpening on: no ghost.
+5. TrackView lists the three new properties. RenderDoc: PostAA composite +2 samples only, DOF
+   downscale/composite unchanged in pass count.
+
+## 5. Docs
+
+`README.md` (Lens table), `docs/ConsoleReference.md` (`r_LensChromaticAberration`), both
+English. Spec listed in the README's spec section.
